//! Brain repos — kyma's memory exposed as Git-clonable Obsidian vaults.
//!
//! A *brain* is a bare git repository served by `kyma serve` over smart HTTP
//! at `/git/<name>.git`. Its working tree is an Obsidian vault rendered
//! deterministically from the memory graph (scoped by a realm selector),
//! regenerated by a recurring export job, and accepting `git push` whose
//! markdown edits flow back into memory.
//!
//! This crate is the pure core: vault planning ([`vault`]), note rendering
//! ([`notes`]), MOC/index generation ([`moc`]), the git-binary wrapper
//! ([`gitbin`]), export orchestration ([`export`]), push-ingest planning
//! ([`ingest`]), pkt-line framing for the smart-HTTP advertisement
//! ([`pktline`]), and the registry types ([`registry`]). No axum, no sqlx —
//! `kyma-server` and `kyma-local` provide the HTTP surface, persistence, and
//! memory-table IO around it.

